 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls**
-*   **Precision:** Using `Float32Array` is standard, but large grid offsets may cause floating-point precision issues in vertex positions [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Boundary Conditions:** The offset calculation assumes a centered grid; incorrect offset leads to misaligned voxels [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Degenerate Input:** If instance data is not aligned to 4-byte boundaries or if attribute divisors are not set correctly, rendering will fail or produce garbage [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Boundary Conditions:** The offset calculation assumes a centered grid; incorrect offsets misalign voxels [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Attribute Alignment:** Instance data must be properly aligned and divisors must be set to 1 to associate one instance attribute with multiple vertices [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Dynamic Updates:** If instance data changes per frame, buffers must be re-uploaded or mapped appropriately to avoid stale geometry [S2, unofficial].
 
